                        "form": "die Füllhörner"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0707b6e8-f873-3902-a778-998f85f1609e",
                        "entry_id": "f4f53f38-a668-3799-ac4d-b00dc417faa5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "das Horn der Nymphe Amalthea, aus dem sich Reichtum und Segen ergießt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Altgriechische Sage"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d79972f5-c5f7-42d5-8d5b-a23739aa0081",
                                "sense_id": "0707b6e8-f873-3902-a778-998f85f1609e",
                                "text": "In der Kunst wird das Füllhorn häufig mit Blumen und Früchten gefüllt dargestellt."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3d703b75-caaf-3310-96c5-581d5b244dd0",
                        "entry_id": "f4f53f38-a668-3799-ac4d-b00dc417faa5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Überfluss"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figurative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10111234-d1e5-4242-b329-bc3804e36146",
                                "sense_id": "3d703b75-caaf-3310-96c5-581d5b244dd0",
                                "text": "Das Füllhorn dient als Symbol des Überflusses schlechthin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bd0be7b-9651-4637-a4ac-757a43713c19",
                                "sense_id": "3d703b75-caaf-3310-96c5-581d5b244dd0",
                                "text": "„Eine Wunderkammer glich einem Füllhorn an Kuriositäten.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1c70029-a0a7-4ac5-bd6b-0a8c3f2f2cc4",
                                "sense_id": "3d703b75-caaf-3310-96c5-581d5b244dd0",
                                "text": "„Sie erklärte mir die Unterschiede in der Kleidung der Sámi verschiedener Gebiete, ein Füllhorn an Wissen um Traditionen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4324d10e-2ccd-4008-8dcc-416e0bfd527c",
                                "sense_id": "3d703b75-caaf-3310-96c5-581d5b244dd0",
                                "text": "„Minni schüttete ihr Füllhorn an Liebreiz großzügig über die Männerwelt des Moka Efti aus.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c321522-4337-4759-8594-938aabdf570a",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4f53f38-a668-3799-ac4d-b00dc417faa5",
                        "source_sense_id": "0707b6e8-f873-3902-a778-998f85f1609e",
                        "source_sense_description": "Altgriechische Sage: das Horn der Nymphe Amalthea, aus dem sich Reichtum und Segen ergießt",
                        "target_lang_word": "cornucopia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cornucopia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                        "entry_id": "e6d37d4e-5f0e-3981-956c-780cd5be1a29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A goat's horn endlessly overflowing with fruit, flowers and grain; or full of whatever its owner wanted: or, an image of a such a horn, either in two or three dimensions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51479576-1a73-43f0-b87d-01efda93204d",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "Device, an anchor held by a hand from the clouds: behind the anchor are a kind of brackets, in the form of cornucopiæ, croſſed; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aefbaa0-1e25-4c08-b2d0-04993835d5c7",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "It soon came: as they were on their way to a transparency of their majesties, not a little larger than life—with Bellona, in a very handsome helmet, on one side, and Peace, with a cornucopia and a full blown wreath of roses, on the other—the path was interrupted by a little knot of gentlemen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7fa15e9-8131-417d-89d1-b8eb3d36d6ab",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "So far as Swedenborg’s elucidation extends, it is comprised in seven groupings of this family; and, possibly, the Hebraic forms of the several names which are included in them, may at some future period, like so many cornucopiæ of wisdom, yield abundance of precious fruit to the Biblical student."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5309fcaa-dd43-4ecc-a6c0-5c380dff1cdf",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "A head of Trajan, between two cornucopiæ, under which is a winged foot, with a caduceus and a dolphin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b74e371f-28af-448a-819c-79b8ddced739",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "On these the details of the cornucopiae resemble those familiar in the Hellenistic world: from the horn, filleted and filled to overflowing with bunches of grapes, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85b71a89-df5d-4f97-b9eb-4cdd2113d700",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "The three cornucopiae which branch out to hold the candles are apparently unparalleled and this in itself offers some encouragement for regarding the pieces as by Giuseppe, for the majority of his designs seem to have been cast once only (counting for this purpose a pair as a unique item, as with the lower parts of the Victoria and Albert Museum firedogs)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8576d62c-3262-4aaf-a124-68afa6f08217",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "There are other mysteries expressed by the bison horn, the Paleolithic original of which the classical cornucopia is a copy: the horn of plenty is the universal vulva from which emerge all the creatures of life, plants, animals, and humans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32ea7a57-b748-4382-b819-e6839e69ab8a",
                                                "sense_id": "febf0540-8921-3cb4-abd1-05dc16c8720b",
                                                "text": "The two cornucopiae carried by the figure likely identify her as Isis, but they also make clear her inanimate status."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9436a573-1b56-3c14-b939-a496a080af0c",
                                        "entry_id": "e6d37d4e-5f0e-3981-956c-780cd5be1a29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hollow horn- or cone-shaped object, filled with edible or useful things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72e21e77-afb1-32b0-bdcc-95f270ffdfa5",
                                        "entry_id": "e6d37d4e-5f0e-3981-956c-780cd5be1a29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abundance or plentiful supply."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9737652b-d2d5-46e5-9f21-db2a1b10e38a",
                                                "sense_id": "72e21e77-afb1-32b0-bdcc-95f270ffdfa5",
                                                "text": "The store provided a veritable cornucopia of modern gadgets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "368bbd6f-22b5-4fed-b391-a58fa190386e",
                                                "sense_id": "72e21e77-afb1-32b0-bdcc-95f270ffdfa5",
                                                "text": "These days, thanks to the cornucopia of online dance classes and tutorials, you can almost imagine yourself to be a dancer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05527da6-de45-4921-bf11-098b1e73ccfb",
                                                "sense_id": "72e21e77-afb1-32b0-bdcc-95f270ffdfa5",
                                                "text": "The bulk of the benefits were flowing to China, which became the low-cost producer for the developed world, and to consumers in advanced economies whose shops offered a cornucopia of cheaper goods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ca4150e-900b-418d-9bc3-51db78b9df7c",
                                                "sense_id": "72e21e77-afb1-32b0-bdcc-95f270ffdfa5",
                                                "text": "Despite its sparse syntax, the expressiveness and flexibility of the λ-calculus make it a cornucopia of logic and mathematics. The Lambda Calculus (Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6acea10e-6a92-4a09-91db-98f13264ae34",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4f53f38-a668-3799-ac4d-b00dc417faa5",
                        "source_sense_id": "0707b6e8-f873-3902-a778-998f85f1609e",
                        "source_sense_description": "Altgriechische Sage: das Horn der Nymphe Amalthea, aus dem sich Reichtum und Segen ergießt",
                        "target_lang_word": "corne d’abondance",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "corne d’abondance",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1793d5c2-ce84-3115-b055-1ddee66e3a83",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44ce38-6acc-3d09-a712-4ee5843b4219",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Corne de la chèvre Amalthée, nourrice de Jupiter, de laquelle il avait voulu, pour récompense, qu’il sortît sans cesse une abondance de toutes sortes de biens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mythologie grecque"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd97400b-829d-4e0a-a3b5-eb3475fec3da",
                                                "sense_id": "1793d5c2-ce84-3115-b055-1ddee66e3a83",
                                                "text": "Il le dépeignait tenant en main la corne d’abondance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f898779f-1d4a-4218-bdf3-90c8aacca45e",
                                                "sense_id": "1793d5c2-ce84-3115-b055-1ddee66e3a83",
                                                "text": "D’augustes déités Qui viennent sur les pas de la belle espérance Verser la corne d’or où fleurit l’abondance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44ce38-6acc-3d09-a712-4ee5843b4219",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Source d’abondantes richesses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a59026a2-5fc1-4d88-b03b-a54c4453299c",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                                "text": "Le prieur m’a fait voir son jardin ; c’est leur corne d’abondance : d’excellente salade, des choux qui font plaisir à voir, et surtout des choux-fleurs et des artichauts, comme il n’y en a pas en Europe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f1dc4ad-eff8-4376-8166-db7ac8c814e6",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                                "text": "Il nous était impossible de parler d’un livre qui s’en prenait à un célèbre promoteur dont la publicité était pour nous une corne d’abondance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e48d225-4b69-4bb1-b8f9-f38f0836ce86",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                                "text": "Très vite, le jeune homme se débarrasse de tout conformisme, de tout carcan pour donner libre cours à une spontanéité prodigieuse de l’esprit. Hugo est une corne d’abondance inépuisable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c721e31-c5c4-43bf-84ac-baeaef383be4",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                                "text": "La Turquie, véritable corne d’abondance, fait le bonheur de tous les genres de voyageurs, des fervents de la nature aux amoureux de la culture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae48861a-100c-4e67-ba04-c41a0a63e1f0",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0b0cc7-9a0f-3ac3-87a7-f5c967cb04ab",
                                                "text": "Une véritable corne d’abondance culturelle a déversé sur la génération du baby boom les merveilles de la nature et de la culture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f772abfb-7aea-32a6-a9c4-0ca250813af3",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44ce38-6acc-3d09-a712-4ee5843b4219",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Le port de Constantinople, parce que le commerce y transportait tous les produits du monde."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62992145-ff27-3768-a4a7-c5c42473335e",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44ce38-6acc-3d09-a712-4ee5843b4219",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Champignon appelé aussi « trompette de la mort »."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44c50143-ce62-38db-ac11-5f21bf084abc",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44ce38-6acc-3d09-a712-4ee5843b4219",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Meuble représentant l’objet mythologique du même nom dans les armoiries. Elle est généralement représentée couchée avec des fruits et légumes sortant de l’embouchure. La liste des éléments remplissant la corne est laissée à la discrétion de l’illustrateur et ne sont jamais blasonnés."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ada18a3d-ddfa-4a88-b165-066779ee80d0",
                                                "sense_id": "44c50143-ce62-38db-ac11-5f21bf084abc",
                                                "text": "D’azur à une corne d’abondance d’or, déversant des fruits au naturel, senestrée d’une croix cléchée et pommetée d’or remplie de gueules, qui est de la commune de Saint-Chinian de l’Hérault → voir illustration « armoiries avec une corne d’abondance »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f5a82fce-b848-4df9-b081-15e0e2691a99",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4f53f38-a668-3799-ac4d-b00dc417faa5",
                        "source_sense_id": "0707b6e8-f873-3902-a778-998f85f1609e",
                        "source_sense_description": "Altgriechische Sage: das Horn der Nymphe Amalthea, aus dem sich Reichtum und Segen ergießt",
                        "target_lang_word": "cornucopia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cornucopia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c7d25dd-9e20-3480-9e9c-1ada0065d3cd",
                                        "entry_id": "1da1fc1a-081b-3947-bffc-1463dc85f9ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Símbolo de prodigalidad. Originalmente se le representaba como cuerno de una cabra (la cabra Amaltea, por la ninfa homónima, pletórico de frutas y flores. Actualmente, una canasta de mimbre ha substituido al cuerno, y verduras y monedas han reemplazado a las flores."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7749db0c-d0a4-4a86-8f4a-0e3aa7a773e9",
                                                "sense_id": "5c7d25dd-9e20-3480-9e9c-1ada0065d3cd",
                                                "text": "La cornucopia o cuerno de la abundancia es uno de los cuernos del dios-río Aqueloo, metamorfoseado en toro, que le fue arrancado por Hércules, cuando luchaba contra él. Según otros, es un cuerno de la cabra con cuya leche la ninfa Amaltea amamantó a Júpiter en su niñez, cuando se ocultó de su padre, Saturno, para que no lo devorase. Se dice que Júpiter se lo arrancó a la cabra jugando, y se lo regaló a Amaltea, asegurándole que el cuerno se llenaría de frutos cada vez que ella lo deseara. La cornucopia es un atributo muy mostrado en las monedas romanas, en manos de divinidades benéficas, como Ceres y Cibeles, o de alegorías como Abundancia y Fortuna"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
